{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261112T041348Z-76de58b6", "ts": "2026-11-12T04:20:22Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.8.2-dev.1", "branch": "feature/bounded-cumulative", "build": "9e93e8bdf2b4"}, "body": {"base_commit": "9e93e8bdf2b49b74c9123fcad6de1e06bbf188d1", "base_tree": "02815e8ff12356c937a6cd197b5be870acf9b592", "head_tree": "2e194cf091c8c0ded6bbd0d711459e761a0bdb72", "head_commit": "9a440188d8757d1958cb62616c0f670aac36c5b9", "dispatch_commit": "9a440188d8757d1958cb62616c0f670aac36c5b9", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md", "plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/critic_mode.py", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/lib/telemetry.py", "plugin/methodology/planning.md", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-cycle.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-protocol.md", "plugin/skills/pr/SKILL.md", "tests/test_bounded_cumulative.py", "tests/test_measure_repeat_cumulative_yield.py", "tests/test_review_stats.py", "tests/test_reviewer_payload_budget.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py", "tools/measure-repeat-cumulative-yield.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/bounded-cumulative-design.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-bounded-cumulative.md", ".prawduct/changes/bounded-cumulative.md", "plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md", "plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/critic_mode.py", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/lib/telemetry.py", "plugin/methodology/planning.md", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-cycle.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-protocol.md", "plugin/skills/pr/SKILL.md", "tests/test_bounded_cumulative.py", "tests/test_measure_repeat_cumulative_yield.py", "tests/test_review_stats.py", "tests/test_reviewer_payload_budget.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py", "tools/measure-repeat-cumulative-yield.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/bounded-cumulative-design.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-bounded-cumulative.md", ".prawduct/changes/bounded-cumulative.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "boundary_frontier's unreadable fallback has no test", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. It broke because the tests cover each decline condition (1-5) and the override, but not the SPAN_FULL_UNREADABLE branches: an unusable store, an unresolvable merge-base, an unreadable HEAD tree, or a failed `rev-list`. The store branch is the reachable one. A clone shared by worktrees on different plugin builds can hold a schema-ahead fact (this session's own probes printed plugin-binary-skew), and `_store_precheck` then makes every cumulative dispatch go full through `precheck[1]`. Nothing pins that path. If the precheck's return shape changes, cumulative dispatch on such a clone raises instead of falling back, and no test fails. That fallback is the evidence behind the plan's 'authority fails closed \u2192 conforms; any frontier condition that declines falls back to the full span' disposition. Fix: add a test in tests/test_bounded_cumulative.py that writes a schema-ahead (or corrupt-store) fact, then asserts `boundary_frontier` returns status full with code SPAN_FULL_UNREADABLE, and that `begin_review` records `span_reason` 'unreadable'. Watch the test fail with the precheck branch removed.", "files": ["plugin/lib/gates.py", "tests/test_bounded_cumulative.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "Cumulative-interval prose still promises the full span beside the new bounded paragraph", "recommendation": "Class. Why it broke: Chunk 03 added the bounded paragraph next to the sentences it falsifies instead of correcting them. The core rule 'A mechanism change is done when every artifact DESCRIBING it agrees ... delete superseded sentences ... rather than adding beside them' applies, and the plan's Chunk 03 says it 'corrects every sentence Chunk 02 made false by claiming a cumulative spans merge-base...HEAD'. Two instruction-file members survive. (1) review-cycle.md \u00a7 'Cumulative mode and the PR gate', the paragraph right above 'A repeat cumulative is bounded'. It still says critic-begin 'derives the interval merge-base tree \u2192 HEAD's tree \u2014 deliberately spanning every commit on the branch, so cross-chunk integration cracks surface', and that this shared resolver means 'reviewer and gate never diff different ranges'. A bounded repeat now diffs frontier \u2192 HEAD while the gate diffs merge-base \u2192 HEAD, and the cross-chunk guarantee is exactly what bounding trades away. A builder who reads this has no reason to ask for `cumulative full` before a risky merge. (2) SKILL.md step 4, the exit-3 paragraph: 're-dispatch as `cumulative`, whose interval IS the gate's span. For `cumulative` and `verify-resolutions` the two intervals coincide'. That stops being true once the span is bounded; the conclusion still holds only because of frontier condition 5. Remedy: make both statements relational (the interval starts at merge-base, or at the boundary frontier when one stands, and the composed coverage is what equals the gate's span) and move the cross-chunk rationale onto the `full` override. To make the literal survivors mechanical, record the retired phrasing as `retires:` on a project-state design decision so `retired-claim-survives` finds the next one. Search `merge-base`, `whole branch`, `every commit on the branch`, `gate's span` and `coincide` across plugin/skills and plugin/methodology, not only the tokens already edited.", "files": ["plugin/skills/critic/review-cycle.md", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "'files_context ... read, never rated' leaves open whether a delta-caused stale description in an already-reviewed file can be reported", "recommendation": "Class (Framework Check 8, Instruction Clarity). Why it broke: the new third file set has an absolute 'never rated' stated in two places (review-protocol.md's `cumulative` bullet; review-cycle.md's 'read and rated by no pass'). It does not say how that rule interacts with Goal 4's drift rule, which follows 'a description whose subject moved' and is expected to name sites outside the diff. One reviewer will treat 'delta file Y changed behaviour, and bundle file X in files_context still describes the old behaviour' as a finding about Y. Another will drop it because X is context. That case is stale prose an earlier-changed file still carries, the biggest named residual-loss class once the sweep was cut (4 of the 7 same-base losses in the plan's Chunk 01 reading). The design's own \u00a7 Limits assumed a bounded reviewer 'may raise the same finding from there'. Under one reading the protocol forbids that recovery, so the loss #1153 measures would be partly self-inflicted. A second gap in the same class: no reviewer-facing contract surface mentions files_context at all. SKILL.md step 5's subject/oracle split, coordinator.md's dispatch template ('Read files_reviewed ... and files_oracle') and agents/critic-reviewer.md step 6 name only the two old sets, so a dispatched reviewer learns about the bundle's other files from one clause in the Modes bullet. Remedy: state the rule relationally in the one home, review-protocol.md 'Scope and Stage'. A context file is never rated on its own merits; a finding the DELTA caused (a description in a context file that the delta made false) has the delta file as its subject, rated in full, and names the context site. Then point the reviewer contract surfaces at that home rather than enumerating two sets.", "files": ["plugin/skills/critic/review-protocol.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-cycle.md"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "rule-unenforced: mid-build rulings are appended to the plan's decision log and never cascaded into the sections they overturn, so the lever's falsifier still reads the superseded ~1% baseline", "recommendation": "The rule is written: 'Recording a scope narrowing (chunk deferred, work cut) is a CASCADE: plan bodies INSTRUCT against the changed fact' (learnings/authoring.md), with its sibling 'A ruling recorded only where the deciders read it is NOT recorded'. No check owns it: `retired_claims` only reads `Retires:` declarations on `## Direction` norms and project-state decisions, never a build plan's 'Decisions made mid-build' entries. The load-bearing member: the Chunk 01 re-derivation in the plan puts the same-base blocking loss at about 7 in 114 (about 6%), not about 1%, and bounded reviews only ever run on same-base rows. But the falsifier, in both `bounded-cumulative-design.md` ('Falsifies the lever') and the plan's Goals ('Falsifier (from the design)'), still retires the lever at a rate 'well above the ~1% measured'. `plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md` sends the #1153 measurer to that falsifier, and the change record says the measurement is 'against the design's falsifier'. Read as written, the expected result already trips it, so whoever runs #1153 either retires a lever that works as predicted or quietly reinterprets the threshold. Other members with the same cause: the plan's `**Level:** Medium` still names Chunk 01's sweep replay as the step that would raise it, though that replay is done and the real open risk is the #1153 loss measurement. The design's 'What the reviewer gets' still hands the bundle over as oracle (corrected to `files_context` in Chunk 03) and still lists the rated sweep as an addition. Its Build shape still names `coverage.boundary_frontier` and the sweep. Its frontmatter `status:` still says 'NOT to be built'. Plan Chunk 02's Tests bullet still says 'the rest of the bundle rides as oracle'. Two `governed_by` dispositions (local-first; never specific to Python) still rest on the sweep, which was never built. Scope: class. Fix the members by restating the falsifier against the same-base baseline, either with the number re-attached and its re-deriving command (`tools/measure-repeat-cumulative-yield.py <repo>`) or relationally, and by bringing Level and the superseded design sections into line with the rulings. To close the class, let a plan's mid-build decision carry a `Retires:` field that `retired_claims` reads, so a superseded phrasing ('~1% measured', 'rides as oracle') is found where it survives.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/bounded-cumulative-design.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-bounded-cumulative.md"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "record-lint change-fragment: .prawduct/changes/bounded-cumulative.md", "recommendation": "missing-consumer-note: add `## Consumer note` with the text for consumers, or `none: <reason>` when there is nothing to tell them", "files": [".prawduct/changes/bounded-cumulative.md"], "source": "record-lint", "fid": "R-5"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 5, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "'a superseded blocker still clears only through a full span' is false for blockers after the frontier", "recommendation": "Condition 5 checks only merge-base \u2192 frontier. Take a chunk review C1 after frontier A whose blocker is superseded by a later review C2. A bounded cumulative over A.tree \u2192 HEAD then composes mb \u2192 A \u2192 HEAD and never stands at C1's tree, so C1's blocker clears through a bounded span. That is sound, and it matches what the gate's 'run /prawduct:critic cumulative' remedy promises. But review-cycle.md's 'A repeat cumulative is bounded' paragraph and the `boundary_frontier` docstring ('only a review spanning the whole bundle may clear one it supersedes') say only a full span can clear a superseded blocker. An operator who believes that may pay for a `cumulative full` the lever exists to save. Make the claim relational: blockers at or before the frontier force a full span. Instance.", "files": ["plugin/skills/critic/review-cycle.md", "plugin/lib/gates.py"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "SKILL.md exit-3 text still says cumulative's interval IS the gate's span", "recommendation": "Chunk 03's deliverable was to correct every sentence Chunk 02 made false by claiming a cumulative spans merge-base...HEAD. SKILL.md step 4's exit-3 paragraph still reads 're-dispatch as `cumulative`, whose interval IS the gate's span' and 'For `cumulative` and `verify-resolutions` the two intervals coincide'. A bounded interval is frontier \u2192 HEAD. The action the sentence prescribes is still right: a bounded exit 3 composes with the frontier's clean path, and condition 5 guarantees that path, so stopping is correct. Make the sentence relational ('composes to the gate's span') rather than 'IS'. Instance.", "files": ["plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "A records-only delta since the frontier exits 3 before the bundle relays run", "recommendation": "For a bounded cumulative whose delta holds no judgeable file, the free-interval refusal in begin_review fires before `_proposed_chunks` and `record_lint` run. An explicit repeat `cumulative` after a records-only edit therefore grades no record. Before this change it ran a full span with record-lint. The plan's mid-build decision justifies exit 3 by composition only, not by the owner's 'every machine relay grades merge-base \u2192 HEAD' ruling. The /prawduct:pr flow already passed records-only deltas without a review, so the practical loss is small. Either name the relay consequence in the decision or pin the behaviour with a test. Nothing pins it today.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "Two governed_by dispositions cite reasons the diff no longer contains", "recommendation": "Governing-Artifact Reconciliation: every disposition is true of the diff as to conformance. Two of their stated reasons are stale. 'proportionality ratchets both ways \u2192 conforms; Chunk 04 measures the yield': Chunk 04 ships the `by_span` instrument and files the measurement as #1153. 'local-first \u2192 conforms; the sweep is `git grep -F`': no sweep is built, and only the tool's replay greps. Conformance still holds in both cases (the instrument is local, and the measurement is filed with its method), so this is not a departure. Covered: nonfunctional-requirements (4), architecture (8) and data-model (8) dispositions.", "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Error-path coverage of the bounded dispatch is thin but present", "recommendation": "The decline paths are tested one condition at a time (including path-not-clean through a blocker, a resolved blocker, a sibling lineage and a blocked newest review), along with the override and the end-to-end composition to `check_cumulative_critic`. The `cannot diff the bundle` refusal in begin_review is untested. It is the same direction as the existing `cannot diff` refusal, so no edit is wanted beyond the WARNING above.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "The `full` override travels as a provenance string", "recommendation": "begin_review decides the span by testing `--chosen-by` for exact equality with critic_mode.FULL_SPAN_RATIONALE. `mode_chosen_by` is a provenance field; other rationales embed extra text (`explicit-args final redirected: ...`), and an edit that annotates this one the same way would silently turn off the override. The shared constant contains the risk today. If the rationale ever gains detail, put the test behind one predicate in critic_mode (e.g. `requests_full_span(chosen_by)`) instead of comparing strings at the call site.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/critic_mode.py"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "A rebased branch's span_reason reads `no-boundary-review`, not `base-moved`", "recommendation": "Lineage is membership in merge-base..HEAD, so after a rebase the pre-rebase boundary facts look like a sibling branch's and are skipped. The full span is still correct, but by_span's `reasons` will file base advances made by rebasing under `no-boundary-review`. Note this when #1153 reads the reason counts; no code change is asked for now.", "files": ["plugin/lib/gates.py"], "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "The yield tool re-derives the prior review and does not read the recorded span", "recommendation": "tools/measure-repeat-cumulative-yield.py `_find_prior` approximates the frontier (newest strictly-ancestral cumulative, no condition 5, base_reviewed equality). The docstring calls that 'the review a bounded dispatch would have started from'. Facts now record the real answer (`span`, `bounded_from`). The falsifier's second clause, old-only blockers found after BOUNDED rows, cannot be answered without telling bounded rows from full ones. Before #1153 runs, have the tool read `span`/`bounded_from` where present instead of keeping a second derivation of the frontier.", "files": ["tools/measure-repeat-cumulative-yield.py"], "oid": "O-8"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "Bounded-state discriminators in begin_review are mixed", "recommendation": "`relay_files` branches on `bundle_files is not None`, while `relay_base_commit`/`relay_base_tree` branch on `span == SPAN_BOUNDED`. Today the two agree by construction (two signals, one function). Using `span` for all three keeps them from drifting apart.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py"], "oid": "O-9"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "Span vocabulary is copied as literals in telemetry", "recommendation": "telemetry `_SPANS = (\"bounded\", \"full\")` and the `'bounded' if ... else 'full'` grouping copy critic_consolidate.SPAN_VALUES. This follows the existing `_STAGES` pattern, so no change is wanted unless that pattern is revisited.", "files": ["plugin/lib/telemetry.py"], "oid": "O-10"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "The `full` clause in the precedence list's first item is placed before the general rationale it qualifies", "recommendation": "In review-cycle.md precedence item 1, the `cumulative full` sentence sits between 'an explicit mode argument' and 'Rationale: \"explicit-args\" \u2014 except ...', so the general rationale reads as if it follows the exception. Moving it after the existing except-clause would make the item scan in order. Wording only.", "files": ["plugin/skills/critic/review-cycle.md"], "oid": "O-11"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "boundary_frontier reports a failed rev-parse of a fact's base_reviewed as base-moved", "recommendation": "`_tree_of` returns None when `git rev-parse <base_reviewed>^{tree}` fails. None never equals the merge-base tree, so the fact sets `base_moved` and the dispatch can decline with `SPAN_FULL_BASE_MOVED` when the real cause is `SPAN_FULL_UNREADABLE`. Coverage is safe because a full span is today's behaviour, but `by_span.reasons`, the instrument #1153 reads, would miscount it. This is rare, since the base commit is normally an ancestor of HEAD. Scope: instance. Branch on a None tree to the unreadable code.", "files": ["plugin/lib/gates.py"], "oid": "O-12"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "the yield tool's git helpers read a failed git call as an empty answer", "recommendation": "`Git.removed_lines`, `Git.blob` and `Git.grep_files` in `tools/measure-repeat-cumulative-yield.py` ignore the return code. A failing diff, show or grep (exit 2) therefore looks the same as 'no removed lines' or 'no hit', which is the 'missed' answer the Decision 2 re-ruling rested on. The fix round's non-zero catches under `--vanished-in source` show the instrument can return non-zero, and #1153 needs the classification path, which does check `changed()`'s return code. So nothing decided is at risk today. Counting git failures in the report would make a degraded run visible.", "files": ["tools/measure-repeat-cumulative-yield.py"], "oid": "O-13"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "the Signals line gained a Span field, but two reviewer-side surfaces still describe the three-field shape", "recommendation": "`plugin/agents/critic-reviewer.md:31` and `plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md:11` describe the rendered line as `Stage \u00b7 Judgeable files \u00b7 Type`. `signals_line` now appends `\u00b7 Span: \u2026` on a cumulative, and neither surface mentions `files_context`. The meaning reaches reviewers through `review-protocol.md`'s cumulative bullet, so no reviewer misreads its subject. This is a downstream consumer of the changed contract that was not swept. Make those descriptions relational (for example, 'the code-rendered signals line') rather than listing the fields.", "files": ["plugin/agents/critic-reviewer.md", "plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md"], "oid": "O-14"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "Records Pass coverage", "recommendation": "Rated all three of `files_oracle` against the three bars: `.prawduct/artifacts/bounded-cumulative-design.md`, `.prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-bounded-cumulative.md` and `.prawduct/changes/bounded-cumulative.md`. The change fragment's claims about frontier, interval, relays, Signals and by_span match the code, so nothing shipping is false there; its missing consumer note is record-lint's and is not restated here. The design and plan members above clear the 'misleads into action' bar through the falsifier. The rest of their staleness, taken alone, would not.", "oid": "O-15"}], "duration_seconds": 540, "scope": "bounded-cumulative", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["02", "03", "04"], "chunks_proposed": ["02", "03", "04"], "chunk": "02", "base_reviewed": "9e93e8bdf2b49b74c9123fcad6de1e06bbf188d1", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/bounded-cumulative-design.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-bounded-cumulative.md", ".prawduct/changes/bounded-cumulative.md", "plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md", "plugin/methodology/planning.md", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-cycle.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-protocol.md", "plugin/skills/pr/SKILL.md"], "chunk_graded": "02", "chunks_graded": ["02", "03", "04"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-bounded-cumulative.md", "findings": [{"check": "change-fragment", "path": ".prawduct/changes/bounded-cumulative.md", "line": null, "detail": "missing-consumer-note: add `## Consumer note` with the text for consumers, or `none: <reason>` when there is nothing to tell them"}], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 1, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-12T04:13:53Z"}}

